+# Attention Record Client Boundary
+
+Status: prerequisite boundary only. The four-kind current-report UI and HLA #1593
+remain open. This document records the client contract introduced on canonical
+`b2d0fe393ac0971e906cce275e91f45e94422593`; it does not claim a new human style
+approval or a completed product surface.
+
+## Scope
+
+- `apps/web/frontend/lib/attention-key.ts` owns the dependency-free whole-item key codec.
+- `apps/web/frontend/lib/attention-record.ts` reads one authorized source record for
+  `anomaly`, `upcoming_cost`, `contract_review`, or `contract_renewal`.
+- `apps/web/frontend/ui-contracts/attention-current-report/` reuses the frozen
+  existing default-shell style triplet. Those bytes are copied unchanged and are
+  frozen style reuse, not a claim of new human approval.
+- `backend.ts`, generated contracts, API routes, auth, pages, and reporting services
+  are unchanged. The reader calls the existing `backendRequest` transport with the
+  four generated literal record paths.
+
+## Key codec
+
+`encodeAttentionKey` emits the complete UTF-8 bytes of a nonempty well-formed Unicode
+string as canonical unpadded base64url. Empty input, non-strings, and unpaired
+surrogates throw `TypeError`; bytes are never silently replaced. `decodeAttentionKey`
+returns `null` for non-strings, empty input, padding, characters outside the base64url
+alphabet, impossible lengths, noncanonical tail bits, invalid UTF-8, or a decoded empty
+string. It never splits a key, guesses a prefix, folds case, or parses an identity.
+
+## Reader contract
+
+The reader validates kind and decodes the route key before any request, so invalid
+values return `invalid` with zero fetches. A successful response must be an object
+envelope with exactly `item_id` and `rows`, the exact decoded `item_id`, and an array
+of non-null row objects limited to the generated public row fields. Present non-null
+values must match the generated scalar type. Any malformed JSON, unexpected key,
+wrong identity, or wrong scalar type throws a sanitized protocol error; the reader
+never returns `[]`, substitutes a requested ID, or exposes response content in an
+exception. `rows: []` is passed through as a valid empty record under the generated
+contract and does not prove source existence outside API authority.
+
+Row order, duplicate multiplicity, null fields, amount/price strings, and all declared
+public fields are preserved exactly. Missing and null fields remain absent/null for a
+future `Unknown` presentation; no currency, price, total, or recommendation is invented.
+
+## Status handling
+
+| Status | Result |
+|---|---|
+| 200 valid envelope | `ok` with the decoded `item_id` and unchanged rows |
+| 401 | `redirect('/login')`, outside any transport catch |
+| 403 | `denied` |
+| 404 | `not_found` |
+| 503 | `unavailable`, with `retryAfter` only when the header is valid delta-seconds or an HTTP-date |
+| other non-OK | sanitized error |
+| network/JSON/protocol failure | sanitized error |
+
+There is no fallback to a list, first page, alternate source, warehouse, generic detail,
+or a second auth mechanism. Busy and source-unavailable 503 responses are both
+`unavailable`; the safe `Retry-After` header is transport metadata, not copy rendered
+verbatim.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+This prerequisite adds no user-visible queue, detail view, ranking, feed handling, or
+per-kind UI. Cashflow month is not a record observation. The follow-on UI must be
+measured independently under M700 and still needs real Next and authenticated API
+evidence, controlled failure fixtures, accessibility/visual checks, deployment health,
+and product smoke.
